WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:07.910
So in the last 24 hours, we have seen these
allegations made coming out of Michael Schmidt's

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:15.059
forthcoming book that when Donald Trump was
rushed to Walter Reed Medical Center in 2019,

00:00:15.059 --> 00:00:18.680
it was not that he decided to get ahead on
his 20-20 physical.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:22.520
We suspected that from day one because it
didn't make any sense. But Michael Schmidt

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:27.730
is saying that something medical was taking
place and that it was serious enough that

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:33.440
Mike Pence was told in case Trump has to be
put under anesthesia, be on standby, be ready

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:40.789
to take the helm as as as temporary president
of the United States. So Donald Trump raised

00:00:40.789 --> 00:00:48.569
without prompting that he didn't really have
a stroke on that day. Now, that was weird

00:00:48.569 --> 00:00:52.609
because it hasn't been alleged that Trump
had a stroke on that day. But let's put the

00:00:52.609 --> 00:00:56.820
Trump piece aside and focus on Mike Pence.
Now, Mike Pence was interviewed yesterday

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.850
on Fox News by Bret Baer. Bret Baer, to his
credit, asks the simple and straightforward

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.730
question. Is it true that you were put on
standby in case Donald Trump had to be put

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.340
under anesthesia that day? The answer does
not inspire confidence. Take a look at what

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:14.130
Mike Pence had to say.
The candidate from another party. This refers

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:17.780
to Michael Schmidt's book where he says the
president went to Walter Reed, which in fact

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.960
happened in November of last year. He says
in the book that you were put on alert to

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:30.299
take control, to take office, essentially
if he went under for anesthesia. Is that true?

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:35.950
President Donald Trump is in excellent health.
And Bret, I'm always informed of the president's

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:41.469
movements and whether it was on that day or
any other day and for him. But there was no

00:01:41.469 --> 00:01:47.380
there was nothing out of the ordinary about
that moment or or that day. And I just refer

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.009
the other questions to the White House physician
as far as being on standby.

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:56.619
So the question is, were you put on alert
in case Trump needed to be put under general

00:01:56.619 --> 00:02:02.340
anesthesia? And Mike Pence doesn't say no.
Mike Pence says Trump is an excellent. Health,

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.649
I I'm always informed as to where Trump is
and what Trump is doing, and nothing out of

00:02:07.649 --> 00:02:12.510
the ordinary took place and go talk to the
White House doctor about how healthy Donald

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:18.099
Trump is, not an answer that inspires confidence.
In fact, when I hear Mike Pence say anything

00:02:18.099 --> 00:02:24.349
but know, what I'm hearing is yes. But Bret
Beyer tries again. Take a look at what happened.

00:02:24.349 --> 00:02:30.400
As far as being on standby, I don't I don't
recall being told to be on standby. I I was

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.150
informed that the president had a doctor's
appointment, and I want that. I must do it,

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.629
but I just want to go. I got to tell you,
part of this job is you're always on standby

00:02:41.629 --> 00:02:48.659
is your vice president of the United States.
But the American people can be confident that

00:02:48.659 --> 00:02:55.450
this president is in remarkably good health.
And every single day I see that energy and

00:02:55.450 --> 00:03:04.780
high relief on talk of I don't recall being
told to be on stand by, says Mike Pence. If

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:10.780
you know how politicians lie and avoid answering
questions. This is Mike Pence making it a

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:19.129
semantic linguistic argument. He doesn't recall
being told. And the word used was not stand

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:24.680
by. That's what Mike Pence wants us to believe.
And then he goes back to this refrain of Trump

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.579
is in great health. These are not denials,
my friends. If I had to sum up what Mike Pence

00:03:29.579 --> 00:03:37.880
is saying, if I run what Mike Pence is saying
through a politician of decoding device, Mike

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.579
Pence is saying, yeah, that's what happened
and I don't want to talk about it. No sane

00:03:41.579 --> 00:03:49.030
person could realistically watch that answer
and think that Mike Pence is answering truthfully.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:54.160
If someone is asked a yes or no question and
they talk and they talk and they talk without

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:59.870
answering the question, then the most likely
answer is the one that would be most embarrassing,

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:06.320
which in this case would be, yes, it is true.
We lied. Trump didn't go to Walter Reed for

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.900
a physical. Trump was abruptly rushed to the
hospital. There was the possibility general

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:16.580
anesthesia would be needed. And I was briefed
to be on alert for that. He starts the answer

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:21.930
with the biggest lie. Think back to that.
He is asked about whether this took place.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:28.720
And he says the president is in great health.
We know that's not true. Donald Trump is obese.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:34.170
He's medicated for high cholesterol. And he
eats a terrible diet of fast food and doesn't

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:41.860
exercise. So it starts with a completely obvious
lie and gets worse from there. So we should

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:48.090
continue to be careful not to make specific
assertions about what happened when these

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:52.509
are not the allegations that anybody within
sight is making. So when Trump denies that

00:04:52.509 --> 00:04:58.100
he had a stroke, we shouldn't say, oh, he
definitely had a stroke, but it should raise

00:04:58.100 --> 00:05:04.110
our suspicion because it hasn't been alleged.
Trump is the one raising the idea of a stroke.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:08.800
And that's what's the biggest red flag here.
Let me know what you think. I'm on Twitter

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.510
at David Pakman.
What do you make of Donald Trump's tweet denying

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:18.010
he had a stroke which had not been alleged?
And Mike Pence refusing to answer the simple

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:19.490
question. Let me know what you think. I'm
on Twitter at David Pakman.

